msgid "Shrink each uploaded image automatically by removing hidden camera data and re-saving with stronger compression. Works on JPEG, PNG, and GIF. Most uploads end up 10 to 30 percent smaller with no visible quality change. If you already use EWWW, Imagify, Smush, or ShortPixel, leave this on; they will run alongside."
msgstr ""

#: dist/wpmediaverse/includes/Admin/Settings/SettingsRegistrar.php:422
#: includes/Admin/Settings/SettingsRegistrar.php:422
msgid "Create WebP copies for faster loading"
msgstr ""

#: dist/wpmediaverse/includes/Admin/Settings/SettingsRegistrar.php:428
#: includes/Admin/Settings/SettingsRegistrar.php:428
msgid "Save a second copy of every image in WebP format. WebP files are about 25 to 35 percent smaller than JPEG, so pages load faster for your visitors. Browsers that support WebP use the smaller file; older browsers keep using the original. Already have older uploads to optimize? Visit a media item and use Re-optimize, or ask your developer to run the bulk optimizer command."
msgstr ""

#: dist/wpmediaverse/includes/Admin/Settings/SettingsRegistrar.php:448
#: includes/Admin/Settings/SettingsRegistrar.php:448
msgid "Create AVIF copies for the smallest possible files"
msgstr ""

#: dist/wpmediaverse/includes/Admin/Settings/SettingsRegistrar.php:454
#: includes/Admin/Settings/SettingsRegistrar.php:454
msgid "Save a third copy of every image in the newer AVIF format. AVIF is around 30 to 50 percent smaller than WebP, so pages load even faster on modern browsers (Chrome, Firefox, Safari 16.4+, Edge). Older browsers fall back to WebP, then the original. Encoding AVIF is much slower than WebP so uploads will take longer. Requires a host with AVIF-capable Imagick or GD; the option will silently no-op if the server cannot encode AVIF."
msgstr ""

